    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter July 26th with a clear top-tier anchor in **Yordan Alvarez** (87.42), whose elite xwOBA of 0.477 and favorable matchup against Fedde make him the clear offensive engine. Joining him at the top of the board is **Colt Keith** (69.64), who leverages a massive +18% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill profile and a +10% lift from leading off to solidify his status as an elite play. **Trea Turner** (67.40) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (62.83) also provide high-upside opportunities, with both benefitting from leadoff positioning and favorable dynamic platoon advantages against their respective right-handed counterparts. While **Caleb Durbin** (55.37) is hampered by wind-in conditions, his potential for base-stealing against a slower-to-the-plate Gausman keeps his value high given the scarcity of speed in our current build.\n\nThe toughest call for today\u2019s lineup was omitting **Carson Benge** (45.90), who served as the final cut from the active roster. While **Carson Benge** projects marginally better than some of our lower-tier starters, the depth of our outfield options and the specific platoon edges provided to **Casey Schmitt** (54.02)\u2014who receives a +11% boost from his dynamic platoon and a favorable wind-out condition\u2014pushed **Casey Schmitt** into the starting lineup for the added power ceiling. Conversely, we are strictly avoiding players falling below the 40.0 efficiency threshold, which kept **Josh Smith**, **Chase Meidroth**, and **Pedro Ramirez** on the bench to preserve our limited game caps for higher-leverage spots. \n\nRisk management remains a priority today, particularly for **Dillon Dingler** (50.06) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (50.69). **Kazuma Okamoto** is battling a -5% penalty due to wind blowing in, and **Dillon Dingler** faces a -15% dynamic platoon hit, signaling that both players occupy the lower end of our starting floor. We are monitoring all lineups closely, as any late-breaking changes to batting orders could shift these efficiency scores significantly. With **Christian Yelich**, **Hyeseong Kim**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Luis Pena** remaining off the active card today, our focus is strictly on maximizing the efficiency of the 13 chosen starters to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 standings.",
